===persian===

خواب می‌بینی
تو دوتاری هستی
من نوازنده بی‌صبر و قراری هستم.
دشت ارژن خاموش
آتشی بر جانم
می‌زنم می‌خوانم
می‌پری از خواب
مانده بر پیکر تو
نقش انگشتانم.

زمستان ۱۳۶۷

===machine===

You are dreaming
You are a dotar (a two-stringed instrument)
I am a restless and impatient player.
Dasht-e Arjan is silent
A fire upon my soul
I play, I sing
You wake from your sleep
Left upon your body
The imprint of my fingers.

Winter 1367

===lantern===

You are dreaming.
You are a dotar —
and I, the player, restless and without rest.
The plain of Arjan, silent.
A fire upon my soul.
I strike the strings, I sing...
You start awake —
and on your body remains
the print of my fingers.

Winter 1367

===translation===

You are dreaming.
You are a dotar,
and I, your player — restless, without rest.
The Arjan plain lies silent,
a fire laid upon my soul.
I strike the strings, I sing.
You startle awake:
left upon your body,
the print of my fingers.

— Winter 1367

===footnotes===

The whole poem is one musical conceit: the beloved is a دوتار (dotar, a two-stringed long-necked lute), the poet the نوازنده (player) who can find no rest. می‌زنم is "I play / I strike [the strings]" — and to play this instrument is to touch her body, so the fingers that worked the strings leave their mark when she wakes. دشت ارژن (Dasht-e Arjan) is a plain and seasonal wetland west of Shiraz, in Fars — its stillness sets the hush the music breaks.
